<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="QueryFlag: Settings" id="QueryFlag-Settings">

    <primary-label ref="queryflag"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Settings: <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path> (DataGrip: <ui-path>Settings | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path>)</p>
        <p>Shortcut: <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>), then search for <code>QueryFlag</code></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Reference for the QueryFlag settings page: the template list, Open console editor, and Allow blank Text.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>The template list and the Open console editor and Allow blank Text options.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Reference for the QueryFlag settings in JetBrains IDEs: the template list, the Open console editor and Allow blank Text options, and storage.</web-summary>

    <p>
        To open the QueryFlag settings, press <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>)
        and select <ui-path>Tools | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path>.
        In DataGrip, select <ui-path>Database | QueryFlag</ui-path>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Settings reference" id="settings-reference">
        <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_settings_page.png" alt="QueryFlag settings page with three templates and the two options" -->
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Template list" id="template-list">
                <p>
                    Lists your templates.
                    Each row shows the database type icon, the template name, and the first 50 characters of the query.
                    If the template's data source is not available in the current project, the row shows
                    "DataSource not found, please check your Databases settings" in red instead of the query.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Use the <control>Add</control>, <control>Remove</control>, and <control>Edit</control> toolbar buttons to manage templates.
                    See <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic"/>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The <control>Query Flag in DB</control> menu lists templates in the order of this list.
                    New templates go to the end of the list, and so does a template that you change.
                    You cannot sort or reorder the list.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="Open console editor" id="open-console-editor">
                <p>
                    Opens the query console that QueryFlag creates for each run in the editor, so you can see and edit the query that ran.
                    Default: off.
                </p>
                <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_console_editor.png" alt="Console editor opened by QueryFlag showing the query with the token replaced" -->
            </def>
            <def title="Allow blank Text" id="allow-blank-text">
                <p>
                    Runs templates when the selection is empty or contains only spaces.
                    When this option is off, QueryFlag skips the run and shows a warning.
                    Default: off.
                </p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Save changes" id="save-changes">
        <p>
            Changes on this page take effect when you click <control>Apply</control> or <control>OK</control>.
            Templates that you create with <control>Add Query Flag</control> in a query console are saved immediately.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Where QueryFlag stores settings" id="storage">
        <p>
            QueryFlag stores its settings for the whole IDE, not per project, in the <path>options</path> folder of the
            <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/directories-used-by-the-ide-to-store-settings-caches-plugins-and-logs.html#config-directory">IDE configuration directory</a>:
        </p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="query_flag.xml" id="storage-templates">
                <p>
                    The templates.
                    Backup and Sync does not sync this file.
                </p>
                <p>
                    To reuse your templates on another computer, copy this file to the same folder there while the IDE is closed.
                    Templates refer to data sources by their ID, so they work only where the same data sources exist,
                    for example in a project whose data sources are shared through version control.
                    Otherwise, edit each template and select its data source again.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="query_flag_settings.xml" id="storage-options">
                <p>The <control>Open console editor</control> and <control>Allow blank Text</control> options.</p>
                <p>If you use <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/sharing-your-ide-settings.html">Backup and Sync</a> (formerly Settings Sync), these options sync with the <control>Tools</control> category.</p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            Uninstalling QueryFlag does not delete these files, so your templates are still there if you install QueryFlag again.
        </p>
        <p>
            A template stores the name, ID, and URL of its data source, but no password.
            The data source in the <control>Database</control> tool window keeps its own connection settings.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Notifications" id="notifications">
        <p>
            QueryFlag shows its warnings in the notification group <control>QueryFlag development</control>.
            To change how they appear, open <ui-path>Settings | Appearance &amp; Behavior | Notifications</ui-path>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

